  "body": "# Desktop Pet v0.4.8 release notes\n\nStatus: unpublished successor; parent-observed source/candidate qualification is recorded below, while immutable publication and installed public acceptance remain pending. Published Core v0.4.7 (source `52514da5115f09aac22de5429c08f7acdd993258`) and genuine legacy bridge v0.3.11 remain immutable. Existing consumer metadata/evidence continue to identify authentic public4.7 assets until new public assets are available and authenticated.\n\nThe successor addresses the retained protocol-2 completed-journal defect: a genuine legacy app can remain blocked by historical completed update records even after its original matching signed helper confirms terminal `completed` / `manager_exited` with installation and application complete. Qualification must establish narrowly scoped historical read compatibility without weakening fresh execution, reservation, native consent or Unknown-manager gates. User journals, pointers and retained helpers must not be rewritten, cleared or replayed.\n\nProducer identities are neutral Core v0.4.8 (protocol 4 / observation 2 / integration API 1) and genuine legacy v0.3.12 (protocol 3 / observation 1 / integration API 1), built from the same approved Core source. The legacy envelope retains its original app, executable and helper names; it is not a renamed neutral binary. Managed Herdr integration remains v0.4.1 at `6d2ac0446f6ecb84f179e21fac3c5b02e07dc8e8`; beta is unchanged.\n\nNo public successor asset digest, tag, release, tap update, consumer materialization or installed public acceptance is claimed by this note. Source gates and actual-profile read-only smoke are recorded below, separately from publication and native migration.\n\n## Actual-profile reproduction before correction\n\nThe actual user Mac's preserved protocol-2 record was verified terminal by its original strictly signed helper: `completed`, `manager_exited`, `installed:true`, `applied:true`. An explicitly approved real Homebrew compatibility upgrade changed the installed source from0.3.6 to genuine0.3.11 without cleanup or history deletion. The new app reached original-profile Herdr/UI/control readiness, but its native Check and migration action remained disabled with **unsupported operation journal protocol**.\n\nThe consumer-visible regression `app_update::tests::historical_completed_journal_allows_fresh_check_without_recovery` was executed before the production correction in the genuine legacy0.3.12 build. One test ran and failed at `service.begin_check().is_some()` (exit101); this reproduces the current checker obstruction, not an installation or manager failure. This does not establish a passing successor or authorize replay of any historical operation.\n\n## Parent-observed successor qualification\n\nThe same legacy consumer regression passed after correction. Full neutral **769 passed / 1 ignored** and genuine legacy **789 passed / 1 ignored** workspace suites passed. Current TypeScript, **62 Bun tests / 746 expectations**, release-note validation, Rust formatting and installer/ingress shell syntax passed. Both real arm64 candidate packages built, passed strict/deep ad-hoc signature verification, and their actual app/helper pairs advertised neutral4/2/API1 and legacy3/1/API1 respectively.\n\nA throwaway executable linked against the corrected legacy coordinator read the **actual preserved user profile**, not a fabricated journal: latest protocol2 Completed/ManagerExited/installed+applied, immutable historical plan bound to the original config/state, null planned Brew candidate and absent old source image. Historical discovery succeeded while strict current operation and plan reads remained rejected. Original latest-pointer, result and plan bytes were unchanged. No actual-profile startup, recovery, reservation or manager execution was performed by this smoke.\n\nThese observations qualify the corrected source and candidate packages only. Immutable release publication, anonymous public-byte qualification, consumer/tap cutover and independently consented actual native migration remain pending.\n"
